{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":4,"prev":"4a63b73b21cacde10ede05d736cb66a93f80860c3e9815d540b7048d911fab2d","at":"2026-09-30T19:12:37.95725Z","type":"node_output","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","data":{"output":{"findings":[{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","start_line":162,"end_line":173,"issue":"The guard accepts a verdict only when the envelope reports num_turns exactly 1 and fails closed (retried, then unparseable) on an absent or zero count, coupling the whole claude-cli transport to one version-dependent envelope field.","consequence":"If an installed claude CLI omits or renames num_turns, every claude-cli judge call burns MaxAttempts and returns a fail-closed verdict with no verdict produced, so reviews routed to claude-cli/ stall - a loud, safe failure but a total outage of that transport.","confidence":57,"severity":"P2"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","start_line":88,"end_line":91,"issue":"Hook isolation rests on a single --settings disableAllHooks overlay, and the comment asserts it covers plugin-provided hooks, whereas the codex arm disables hooks and plugins with two separate flags because they are distinct surfaces there.","consequence":"If disableAllHooks does not also neutralize plugin hooks, a plugin hook can still speak in the judge's session and the num_turns backstop only fires if the continuation also bumps the reported turn count.","confidence":55,"severity":"P2"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","start_line":166,"end_line":175,"issue":"The fail-closed block (CapText, the Parsed/Decision/Confidence reset, the continued-past message, lastErr=nil) reproduces the codex arm's block rather than sharing one helper.","consequence":"A future change to the fail-closed verdict shape or message must be made in two files; if only one is updated the codex and claude arms silently diverge for the same condition.","confidence":55,"severity":"P3"},{"tag":"advisory","file":"internal/f