{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":7,"prev":"18c2b8def9aeb944a5709d33e998dbcf6115c32a83c32975c22b6e5171588d42","at":"2026-09-30T19:12:38.45539Z","type":"delta_applied","state":"discover","iter":0,"node":"discover","data":{"findings":[{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The guard accepts a verdict only when the envelope reports num_turns exactly 1 and fails closed (retried, then unparseable) on an absent or zero count, coupling the whole claude-cli transport to one version-dependent envelope field. If an installed claude CLI omits or renames num_turns, every claude-cli judge call burns MaxAttempts and returns a fail-closed verdict with no verdict produced, so reviews routed to claude-cli/ stall - a loud, safe failure but a total outage of that transport.","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","line":162,"severity":"p2","category":"advisory","source":"lens"},{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] Hook isolation rests on a single --settings disableAllHooks overlay, and the comment asserts it covers plugin-provided hooks, whereas the codex arm disables hooks and plugins with two separate flags because they are distinct surfaces there. If disableAllHooks does not also neutralize plugin hooks, a plugin hook can still speak in the judge's session and the num_turns backstop only fires if the continuation also bumps the reported turn count.","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","line":88,"severity":"p2","category":"advisory","source":"lens"},{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The fail-closed block (CapText, the Parsed/Decision/Confidence reset, the continued-past message, lastErr=nil) reproduces the codex arm's block rather than sharing one helper. A future change to the fail-closed verdict shape or message must be made in two files; if only one is updated the codex and claude arms silently diverge for the same condition.","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","line":166,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"},{"issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The claude arm's new hook isolation and continued-turn guard are documented only in this code comment; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and the CHANGELOG entry for #193 describe user-hook suppression as Codex-only. A maintainer reading the docs of record concludes hook contamination is handled for codex only and may not extend or preserve the claude guard when the judge transports change.","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","line":87,"severity":"p3","category":"advisory","source":"lens"}],"output_hash":"edf1479011e3e3aa094c1a2361a0f8978d9b820aa8033fdcc60415075140e9f8"}}
